SR: So he called her. The telephone called in. They replace him. He took me in. And my sister was sitting. He opened a big door for me. My sister was sitting and learning Hebrew already there. They were trained them to go to--

INT: Israel.

SR: Palestine at that time, you know? And training them to be able to work on farmland. So they taught them the language. And he opened the door. And I looked in.

I've seen her. [SOBBING] Her, she came out, and she dropped, you know? This was the-- the way I found my sister.

Took her back with me. She had an older lady there. She was like a mother to her at that time.

